{"parentUuid":"2314a265-0397-4c35-8b9f-35600e0f1544","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0e75e1c2-9f84-43c4-8006-cccad7102c77","agentId":"a1623904b5d23ad05","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZAhnV2cMKMGPrgSnSBR28","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  A hook fires when the session ends and says why; a non-interactive run\n  reports a generic reason. Whatever the hook prints is not recorded in the\n  transcript. (How long it may run is hook-timeout's, and which reasons a\n  configured matcher selects is hook-matcher-filter's.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionend\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionend-input\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The reasons clear, resume, logout and prompt_input_exit belong to an\n          interactive session (/clear, /resume, a logout, an exit from the\n          prompt). The mock models none, so every session ends with the\n          generic reason.\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#sessionend\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-end\n  cursor:\n    docs:\n      - https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#sessionend\n    runs:\n      - cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal\n    deviations:\n      - adr: modeled-surface\n        statement: >-\n          The mock has no interactive session, and models a run that ends by its\n          script's result, so the sessionEnd reasons window_close, user_close, aborted\n          and error, and the error message that goes with a reason of error, are not\n          modeled: it always says completed.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bbed68b2-380e-4663-956e-f97e91be325a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:18:34.004Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2314a265-0397-4c35-8b9f-35600e0f1544","userType"